During testing found an issue [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-10391|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/RNTL-10391|smart-link]. It will be fixed separately, closing this task as Done.

{color:#ff5630}Update:{color}

{{actual_time_to_order_completed}} is no longer necessary since each event has a timestamp when the order was moved in that state and we only listen for final state events -> we can compute the value as order_final_state_timestamp - order_created timestamp

{{order_creator}} is also provided on the event → not necessary anymore

Proposed wording, 2.2. of the current TnC-s:

{quote}_You are obliged to provide your requisites in course of registration and usage of the platform as prescribed by the applicable legislation and/or our policies. If you are a legal person, you must submit bank account statements where your bank account and name are visible. We are transferring In-app Payment fees to the bank account you have submitted the bank statements. Failing to provide the requisites will result in sanctions prescribed by the applicable legislation._{quote}

Alternative:

{quote}_Failing to provide the requisites will result in suspension of payments to you and/or terminating the agreement._{quote}

*How to show a share ride button?*

!Screenshot 2022-11-08 at 10.33.39.png|width=347,height=120!

these buttons are configured on [the client side|https://github.com/bolteu/ios-app-client/blob/cf980785c472ac6ccd361ce63ffec41fbe5883d2/mTakso/RideHailingProduct/ActiveOrder/ActiveOrder/RideHailingActiveOrderTransformer.swift#L101] from the order status. 

The middle button can be presented as SOS or Contact option for {{driverAccepted}} and {{driverArrivedToClient}} statuses. We show SOS button if there’s an incident.  {color:#ffffff}noIncident{color}

To show a share ride instead of Contact options we need to add a flag that it is a ride for some one else in {{RideHailingActiveOrderResponse}}

