The solution is the same as described in [https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-5568|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/DRX-5568|smart-link].

* handle tap on the map with [https://developers.google.com/android/reference/com/google/android/gms/maps/GoogleMap.OnMapClickListener|https://developers.google.com/android/reference/com/google/android/gms/maps/GoogleMap.OnMapClickListener|smart-link] handling which gives you map coordinates
* convert map coordinates to world coordinates

{noformat}fun worldCoordinate(locatable: Locatable, tileWidth: Double = 256.0, tileHeight: Double = 256.0): WorldCoordinate {
    var siny = sin((locatable.latitude * PI) / 180)
    siny = min(max(siny, -0.9999), 0.9999)
    return WorldCoordinate(
        x = tileWidth * (0.5 + locatable.longitude / 360),
        y = tileHeight * (0.5 - ln((1 + siny) / (1 - siny)) / (4 * PI)),
    )
 }{noformat}

* convert world coordinates into tile pixel position. We need it because the polygon may cover multiple tiles, otherwise, we will have the polygon cut, like on image below
{noformat}val scale = 1 shl zoom
val pixelCoordinateX = floor(coordinates.x * scale).toInt() - x * tileWidth
val pixelCoordinateY = floor(coordinates.y * scale).toInt() - y * tileHeight{noformat}

